OVERALL COMPARISON

All three test messages produced agreement between Gemini and the rule-based baseline for the main issue category, urgency level and recommended team.

The rule-based method was highly predictable because its outputs were based on fixed keywords. This can be useful where the organisation requires strict and explainable classification rules.

Gemini offered an important advantage because it interpreted the meaning and context of the messages rather than only matching specific words. It also generated escalation reasons and short summaries.

However, Gemini may produce different classifications when messages are ambiguous or when context is limited. It also carries risks including hallucination, inconsistent severity assessment and inappropriate escalation.

Based on the experiment, the LLM approach would be suitable for limited pilot use with human oversight. High-risk, uncertain or sensitive messages should be reviewed by a responsible employee before operational action is taken.
